{
  "phrases": [
    "In 1889,",
    "the 300-metre",
    "Eiffel Tower became",
    "one of the",
    "main attractions at",
    "the World's Fair",
    "in Paris.",
    "How did",
    "an exhibition",
    "landmark become",
    "part of",
    "military communications?",
    "Nine years later,",
    "engineer Eugène Ducretet",
    "sent a Morse",
    "code signal",
    "from the tower",
    "to the Panthéon,",
    "a building about",
    "four kilometres away.",
    "Short and long",
    "signals travelled",
    "through the air.",
    "No telegraph",
    "wire was needed",
    "between the",
    "two buildings.",
    "But that experiment",
    "linked two points",
    "within one city.",
    "The French Army",
    "needed radio",
    "communication between Paris",
    "and the fortresses",
    "on the country's",
    "eastern border.",
    "Long-distance communication",
    "required powerful",
    "transmitters,",
    "sensitive receivers",
    "and tall antennas.",
    "The Eiffel Tower's",
    "height could prove",
    "useful.",
    "In 1903, Paris",
    "officials discussed",
